{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex","id":1528427,"title":"W5 Complaint: The Handling of Pentex","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-01-12T11:18:15-08:00","id":1528427,"title":"W5 Complaint: The Handling of Pentex","content":"I'm fairly okay with the W5 update and my big issues are ones that a lot of people are somewhat more ambivalent about (I am a lore junkie and hate whenever the games attempt to divorce themselves from continuity rather embracing it with a vampire's fangs).<br /> <br /> For me, one issue I'd like to discuss I am not happy with is the handling of Pentex.<br /> <br /> I get what W5 was going for by attempting to address the real life ecological devastation and brutally of the world's various corporations with the strong encouragement to (&quot;Just use Walmart and McDonalds where you can&quot;) but I feel like it's a missed opportunity not to have even a sidebar listing all the wonderful evil brands from WTA's long history.<br /> <br /> * Endron<br /> * Magadon<br /> * Black Dog Games<br /> * RED Network\u200b<br /> * O'Tolley's<br /> * King Beer<br /> <br /> I feel like you're losing out on the brands that most of the audience is smart enough to get the parody of. It also enriches the setting by having these discount brands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T11:30:08-08:00","id":1528428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex#post1528427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fairly okay with the W5 update and my big issues are ones that a lot of people are somewhat more ambivalent about (I am a lore junkie and hate whenever the games attempt to divorce themselves from continuity rather embracing it with a vampire's fangs).<br /> <br /> For me, one issue I'd like to discuss I am not happy with is the handling of Pentex.<br /> <br /> I get what W5 was going for by attempting to address the real life ecological devastation and brutally of the world's various corporations with the strong encouragement to (&quot;Just use Walmart and McDonalds where you can&quot;) but I feel like it's a missed opportunity not to have even a sidebar listing all the wonderful evil brands from WTA's long history.<br /> <br /> * Endron<br /> * Magadon<br /> * Black Dog Games<br /> * RED Network<br /> * O'Tolley's<br /> * King Beer<br /> <br /> I feel like you're losing out on the brands that most of the audience is smart enough to get the parody of. It also enriches the setting by having these discount brands.</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely agree with you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T11:59:31-08:00","id":1528433,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I remember that bit... Justin Achilli didn't like the Subsidiaries so they were all removed from W5. I think we'll see the new dynamic for how confronting &quot;Pentex&quot; works in the upcoming Scent Of Decay book.<br /> <br /> The two quotes from the W5 corebook that I think summarize it best are these (from pg 268):<ul><li>&quot;Pentex is also, for the vast majority of its operations, absolutely, unremarkably mundane in its affairs. Ninety-eight percent of what it does doesn\u2019t involve supernatural creatures or malevolent spiritual entities, just toxic runoff and banal worker exploitation.&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Pentex Group does very little directly and by itself \u2014 it prefers simply to own things and collect the revenues those things generate. As such, it\u2019s unlikely for a Garou pack to encounter Pentex itself.\u200b&quot;</li> </ul>So most of the time Pentex is doing mundane stuff and it won't actually be Pentex itself but another mundane company doing mundane stuff supported by Pentex. That's how Pentex is portrayed in W5.<br /> <br /> The thing I never understood with this change in direction for Pentex is how you calibrate that portrayal in light of an extreme faction like the Cult of Fenris. If it isn't the parody-Wyrm-cult-y Endron or Magadon and instead work with completely mundane companies... I mean, is the idea here that you're actually supposed to play a scenario where Garou go into a completely mundane oil-refinery and start killing people...? And you find out that the oil-refinery isn't by chance so close to a caern because behind the scenes Pentex arranged this? But this still leaves the scenario with an abundance of real-world mundane stuff and very little WtA-specific animism and war against the Wyrm. And ignoring the innocent perspective of the company used by Pentex while destroying them is something I would associate more with the extremism of a Cult of Fenris. But if this version of Pentex is always beyond the reach of the PCs, they necessarily would end up just confronting mundane companies who unknowingly do the bidding of Pentex which is beholden to the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> But as I said, there's a scenario in the upcoming Scent Of Decay. This is the summary: &quot;The Break Room: A corporate fulfillment center seeks productivity at a terrible human cost&quot;. Given what abilities Garou have, I wonder how this scenario is supposed to play out according to these writers from Renegade. Are you supposed to play judge, jury, executioner for bad corporate culture? Are you supposed to tear the place to shreds? Do you need to have a heart-to-heart discussion with a Bane Spirit and convince it to go to therapy? I guess we'll see...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T12:16:15-08:00","id":1528435,"title":"","content":"I don't think PENTEX has ever been used well in Werewolf sourcebooks because ultimately the writers could not decide what exactly it was supposed to be. Is it a source of supernatural evil in the world? If so, what are the supernatural horrors being unleased by these individual companies? Sometimes we would get this, but most often not. Is it just roman-a-clefs of real world companies and the ecological, human, or economic harm they do? If so, why involve the supernatural at all? A lot of subsidiaries are just like that. Is it just supposed to be a dark parody or social commentary of various companies? If so, what place does it really have in a game of &quot;savage horror&quot;? To me, these are all separate things and best handled separately.<br /> <br /> So the end result was too often just a poorly written version of evil comic book companies done in a Captain Planet style who did evil things just to do evil things. It didn't help that very often the writers obviously did not understand actual corporate America and often would write things wrong. For example, it's fairly clear that the original writers in 1e Book of the Wyrm understood that the &quot;directors&quot; meant members of the Board of Directors. They were there to look over the interests of the shareowners. They were not management of the company. Whatever agents of the Wyrm managing things in the individual companies had to be someone else. But in the 2e Book of the Wyrm, the writers didn't seem to understand that and seemed to think the directors were part of management and started assigning them all sorts of managerial responsibilities. I understand it's an easy mistake to make, and very young people would have no idea about these things and not have it negatively impact their game. But it did represent a major flaw in a gameline that otherwise was known for its quality.<br /> <br /> So for me, PENTEX and its various subsidiaries were never well presented. The only way I could use it was to ignore what was written, steal what names and concepts I could get from it, and create for more usable and interesting horrors from the raw material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T12:20:25-08:00","id":1528438,"title":"","content":"As Knightingale said, what is the purpose of Pentex-plots now? Is it just trying to solve issues in the board room or as a consultant? Because the game has painted the typical actions against the company as CoF territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T12:24:54-08:00","id":1528441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528433#post1528433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I remember that bit... Justin Achilli didn't like the Subsidiaries so they were all removed from W5. I think we'll see the new dynamic for how confronting &quot;Pentex&quot; works in the upcoming Scent Of Decay book.<br /> <br /> The two quotes from the W5 corebook that I think summarize it best are these (from pg 268):<ul><li>&quot;Pentex is also, for the vast majority of its operations, absolutely, unremarkably mundane in its affairs. Ninety-eight percent of what it does doesn\u2019t involve supernatural creatures or malevolent spiritual entities, just toxic runoff and banal worker exploitation.&quot;</li> <li>&quot;Pentex Group does very little directly and by itself \u2014 it prefers simply to own things and collect the revenues those things generate. As such, it\u2019s unlikely for a Garou pack to encounter Pentex itself.&quot;</li> </ul>So most of the time Pentex is doing mundane stuff and it won't actually be Pentex itself but another mundane company doing mundane stuff supported by Pentex. That's how Pentex is portrayed in W5.<br /> <br /> The thing I never understood with this change in direction for Pentex is how you calibrate that portrayal in light of an extreme faction like the Cult of Fenris. If it isn't the parody-Wyrm-cult-y Endron or Magadon and instead work with completely mundane companies... I mean, is the idea here that you're actually supposed to play a scenario where Garou go into a completely mundane oil-refinery and start killing people...? And you find out that the oil-refinery isn't by chance so close to a caern because behind the scenes Pentex arranged this? But this still leaves the scenario with an abundance of real-world mundane stuff and very little WtA-specific animism and war against the Wyrm. And ignoring the innocent perspective of the company used by Pentex while destroying them is something I would associate more with the extremism of a Cult of Fenris. But if this version of Pentex is always beyond the reach of the PCs, they necessarily would end up just confronting mundane companies who unknowingly do the bidding of Pentex which is beholden to the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> But as I said, there's a scenario in the upcoming Scent Of Decay. This is the summary: &quot;The Break Room: A corporate fulfillment center seeks productivity at a terrible human cost&quot;. Given what abilities Garou have, I wonder how this scenario is supposed to play out according to these writers from Renegade. Are you supposed to play judge, jury, executioner for bad corporate culture? Are you supposed to tear the place to shreds? Do you need to have a heart-to-heart discussion with a Bane Spirit and convince it to go to therapy? I guess we'll see...</div> </div> </div> </div>As much as I love Justin Achilli, I think that was a big mistake on his part.<br /> <br /> I'm going to say that the book doesn't actually make that mistake you're describing though as while they say, 98% of Pentex activities are completely above board legally, the 2% is pretty well described as typical Wyrm-y Wolfram and Hart skullduggery in the subsequent pages in the Antaogonist section.<br /> <br /> We've got First Teams, executive women with eyes of a human fly, possessed monsters, and other evil plots.<br /> <br /> It seems that the idea is that werewolves are so hopelessly outnumbered that they can only really respond to the 2% &quot;Muhwahahaha Evil!&quot; plots of Pentex rather than attempt to deal with their day to day evils of making Oxycodone or whatever the fuck mundane horrors Magadon is up to.\u200b<br /> <br /> At least that's how I read it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T12:31:41-08:00","id":1528442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528438#post1528438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Knightingale said, what is the purpose of Pentex-plots now? Is it just trying to solve issues in the board room or as a consultant? Because the game has painted the typical actions against the company as CoF territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I don't think that's what it does at all. You have a bunch of werewolf hunting teams and evil monster possessed executives in the description. It also describes taking down a subsidiary as an institutional change.<br /> <br /> At its core, Pentex is set up as a narrative antagonist to<br /> force an institutional-level change and also to put an in-<br /> dividual face on the threat and flay it from the executive\u2019s<br /> head. It\u2019s almost always done through proxies, as well \u2014<br /> the Garou probably don\u2019t go to a \u201cPentex headquarters\u201d<br /> and slaughter their way through the building. Rather,<br /> the fronts act as minions and proxies, through a series of<br /> blinds, layers of plausible deniability, and any number of<br /> contractors, so Pentex operations themselves are never on<br /> anything resembling a front line.<br /> <br /> Destroying a Pentex Group operation is effectively<br /> regime change. Sure, the front is a threat and needs to<br /> go, but what happens in the aftermath? For the Garou to<br /> call it even a small victory, how do they ensure that what<br /> happens after eliminating the threat is any better than<br /> the status quo of the operation\u2019s continued functioning?<br /> If the pack is just an agent of destruction rather than an<br /> agent of change, they\u2019ve effectively justified the human<br /> world\u2019s perception of them as blood-spattered monstros-<br /> ities instead of anything resembling Gaia\u2019s champions.<br /> Simply acting destructively is what got the Garou where<br /> they are today \u2014 and has created opportunities to fill<br /> power vacuums and exploit resources Pg. 271<br /> <br /> This isn't quite the radical change that I think some fans are perceiving it as. It's more that you can't beat the Umbrella Corporation by going into its factories and blowing them up. You're instead more likely need to do some Monkeywrencher antics and even then you're going to probably only take down one branch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T12:38:00-08:00","id":1528444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528441#post1528441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As much as I love Justin Achilli, I think that was a big mistake on his part.<br /> <br /> I'm going to say that the book doesn't actually make that mistake you're describing though as while they say, 98% of Pentex activities are completely above board legally, the 2% is pretty well described as typical Wyrm-y Wolfram and Hart skullduggery in the subsequent pages in the Antaogonist section.<br /> <br /> We've got First Teams, executive women with eyes of a human fly, possessed monsters, and other evil plots.<br /> <br /> It seems that the idea is that werewolves are so hopelessly outnumbered that they can only really respond to the 2% &quot;Muhwahahaha Evil!&quot; plots of Pentex rather than attempt to deal with their day to day evils of making Oxycodone or whatever the fuck mundane horrors Magadon is up to.<br /> <br /> At least that's how I read it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's what I mean by that we'll see how Scent Of Decay handles that. Because sure, one way would be to say &quot;And the Garou only deal with that 2% that's absolutely supernatural.&quot; but another way to read that is the book wants to point STs and players to the other 98% instead in the sense of &quot;Normally plots involving Pentex don't have any direct involvement from Pentex and the company that serves as an antagonist is completely mundane )except for being supported by Pentex).&quot;<br /> <br /> The other reason I'm saying this is that this was the pitch from Justin Achilli during the previews (from the Discord Q&amp;A):<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Can you reveal anything about Pentex - eg do they exist as a single entity, do they exist at all, are they intended as a (secondary) antagonist?</b><br /> Pentex Group is very much an active antagonist, but moves to a more from-the-shadows role in its original concept as a holding company. It operates through fronts \u2014 no Pextex van showing up disgorging fomori in Pentex-branded jumpsuits. Instead a local energy company has been putting the river at risk and if you dig deeply enough you'll find that they're owned by Pentex.<br /> <br /> That said, Pentex is playing at a bigger game, and is itself aware of the animistic nature of the world, so they have advantages and perspectives that &quot;just a corprate entity&quot; doesn't.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>What\u2019s Pentex now?</b><br /> More of a holding company funding various activities for its fronts than an active raid-their-headquarters sort of antagonist. There's plenty of Pentex Group activity, but none of it overtly labeled Pentex.<br /> <br /> \u200b<b>What type of changes have occured with major corporations such as Pentex, Endron, Tellus, Black Dog Games, etc?</b><br /> These legacy groups don't exist in W5; the front structure Pentex Group uses is different from the legacy subsidiary structure. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T17:31:32-08:00","id":1528465,"title":"","content":"Agreed. Pentex as it is now just feels tacked-on, and expecting players to use real companies in its stead is just kind of... off? Like you said, players are smart enough to know what these companies are a proxy for, and <i>not</i> having these proxies and roleplaying stuff like, I dunno, firebombing an actual Walmart just feels kind of off-putting. Because now all the actual bad stuff is completely out of reach from your average player. So now why are they even here?<br /> <br /> And I still don't understand what the point was of distancing it from being directly controlled by the Wyrm and instead now just... an evil company with a patron? It's weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T19:02:26-08:00","id":1528467,"title":"","content":"And it's not even the patron it should be, but apparently they don't like the idea of Corporate versions of City Fathers/Mothers in the W5 development team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T19:18:47-08:00","id":1528468,"title":"","content":"I always enjoyed the Subsidiaries quite a bit. First, I liked the idea that most people had no idea what Pentex was. It's sort of like in the real world, few people on the street know YUM! Brands, but everyone knows the companies that part of YUM! Brands. Pentex was able to operate a bit in the shadows because it was always hiding behind its subsidiaries. Importantly, they also put a layer between the character's and the players, like gh0st-fox says. It's one thing to go on a shooting spree through the O'Tolley's. It's a completely different feel when your characters are shooting up a McDonalds. In light of real world problems and issues, the latter feels more in bad taste.<br /> <br /> I understand why Achilli wanted to remove them - the nature of parody and satire innately brings a level of humor into the game that he doesn't feel belongs in W5. Among the old WoD games, Werewolf was absolutely the one with the most humor involved, nearly all of it revolving around Pentex parodies and satire of real life companies. And to some degree, even if you try to play those sorts of parodies straight, they will always inject a tonal change into a game.<br /> <br /> But I don't think that was ever a bad thing though - the humor in W5 was a core part of the game's identity and did a lot to set Werewolf apart, not just from other WoD games, but from other roleplaying games in general. In contrast, W5 feels a lot more generic and lacks a strong identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-12T19:30:29-08:00","id":1528470,"title":"","content":"I'm open to the idea that Pentex alone isn't really necessary, but that would require building heat up for a lot of other Wyrm Influenced Corporations (WICs), and then you get to the uncomfortable-for-PDX detail of &quot;any corporation could easily become a WIC, they're naturally disposed to getting internally fucked up due to their structure and singular, overwhelming drive to produce profit!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T03:23:04-08:00","id":1528476,"title":"","content":"Id probably of had a variety of wyrm tainted corps organizations and institutions, probably some weaver ones as well. Although w5 as a setting is poorly calibrated to war with such an antagonist so the inclusion is an error in that context.<br /> <br /> Although as is typical the writters seem to forget that pentex was <i>fun</i> and the game is supposed to theoretically fun. Why not just have a Elon musk fill in as the big bad if you're going to passive aggressively whine about him anyway? Go all in and make something which may generate some sense of enthusiasm for the setting lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T04:43:10-08:00","id":1528478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528476#post1528476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Id probably of had a variety of wyrm tainted corps organizations and institutions, probably some weaver ones as well. Although w5 as a setting is poorly calibrated to war with such an antagonist so the inclusion is an error in that context.<br /> <br /> Although as is typical the writters seem to forget that pentex was <i>fun</i> and the game is supposed to theoretically fun. Why not just have a Elon musk fill in as the big bad if you're going to passive aggressively whine about him anyway? Go all in and make something which may generate some sense of enthusiasm for the setting lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to the W5 corebook, it supposedly takes extraordinary amounts of Composure (Composure 5) to not buy Twitter at the ridiculous price-point that Elon Musk bought it. Such a bad attempt at a joke lol <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />... If you had set it at Composure 1 then you would have made fun of Elon Musk but like this, the joke doesn't even work...<br /> <br /> In regards to the game being fun, I'm always thinking of Josh Heath's comments that in the playtest for W5 that he participated in the mechanics for Rage had been even more punishing than the version we got in the release. And there's that comment from Outstar about how she had been the ST for a playtest and had been surprised that during the entire game not one player chose to shift into the Crinos Form. That goes to show what the developers were aiming for before the mechanics came into contact with actual players whose reaction prompted the game to tone down its preference for using sticks rather than carrots in its mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T05:02:04-08:00","id":1528480,"title":"","content":"In general, Pentex has always felt a bit too obvious to me. While I can appreciate the parody companies, I rarely see people actually use them or that characters buy stuff from them.<br /> <br /> I prefer to not have a Pentex and instead a bunch of WICs and just regular arse stores that have tainted products due to someone cutting corners somewhere.<br /> <br /> And I actually feel this would work for W5, since its supposed to be very low-key in the stakes department. Though, with there being no good way to detect if something is tainted, regular poison would also work. There was a dog food issue here last year where bunch of dogs died or were paralyzed due to potato mush going bad. That needs no WICs to be horror, especially if the company refuses to help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T05:45:20-08:00","id":1528482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528480#post1528480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I actually feel this would work for W5, since its supposed to be very low-key in the stakes department. Though, with there being no good way to detect if something is tainted, regular poison would also work. There was a dog food issue here last year where bunch of dogs died or were paralyzed due to potato mush going bad. That needs no WICs to be horror, especially if the company refuses to help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in that sense removing Wyrm-sense as a way to detect Wyrm-taint was a mistake, I think. Because Wyrm-taint is a nice little short-hand for why a company is bad. Sure, you could maybe make the bad guy some Dupont chemical plant. But then to explain why what's going on is bad you'd have to get into the actual science of what's going on, like with PFAS, forever-chemicals, Teflon and all that jazz. With Wyrm-taint, you can just quickly explain &quot;This company produces Wyrm-tainted products and of course that's bad. End of story.&quot; You can use Dupont as the inspiration but you don't have to get into all the details of that real-world-problem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T11:40:16-08:00","id":1528489,"title":"","content":"Just putting my two cents in. In my mind, Pentex would not be evil in itself exactly, but a Wyrm weapon it can use on the material plane efficiently, I mean, through its subsidiaries you can get a sense of what it does in the world and how it attacks, for example, and forgive me if I'm just stating the obvious: a film, game or advertising company could be used to cause an effect that encourages violent attitudes like a brainwashing process, beyond information control; food and pharmaceutical companies that contain substances that make people more apathetic, weak and contaminate them with the Wyrm, possibly making them fomori later on; biofuel company that isn't make biofuel, but it's lie will give people a clear conscience to use their product; arms company that discreetly delivers weapons to mercenary troops, or violent groups, that will strengthen the wyrm influence and also make profit; construction companies that choose to build their buildings in areas that should be preserved, so on, use creativity, otherwise you can use the subsidiaries.<br /> <br /> Now you may be thinking that Wyrm could simply influence the owners or representatives of these companies without the need for Pentex. I agree that it could, but I think it's better for the story for you to face one big enemy that follows a pattern than several small ones that appear just because it's convenient at that moment and there are also the examples I mentioned above that could be used together if they were in the hands of one bigger company (basically a script resource), apart from the fact that this is partly the WOD's stance of not placing all the blame on the supernatural, in other words, Pentex has its mundane part that only thinks about making a profit, simple human greed, and its supernatural part that uses its resources to strengthen the wyrm and helps the first part to profit by table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T13:38:56-08:00","id":1528495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528468#post1528468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always enjoyed the Subsidiaries quite a bit. First, I liked the idea that most people had no idea what Pentex was. It's sort of like in the real world, few people on the street know YUM! Brands, but everyone knows the companies that part of YUM! Brands. Pentex was able to operate a bit in the shadows because it was always hiding behind its subsidiaries. Importantly, they also put a layer between the character's and the players, like gh0st-fox says. It's one thing to go on a shooting spree through the O'Tolley's. It's a completely different feel when your characters are shooting up a McDonalds. In light of real world problems and issues, the latter feels more in bad taste.<br /> <br /> I understand why Achilli wanted to remove them - the nature of parody and satire innately brings a level of humor into the game that he doesn't feel belongs in W5. Among the old WoD games, Werewolf was absolutely the one with the most humor involved, nearly all of it revolving around Pentex parodies and satire of real life companies. And to some degree, even if you try to play those sorts of parodies straight, they will always inject a tonal change into a game.<br /> <br /> But I don't think that was ever a bad thing though - the humor in W5 was a core part of the game's identity and did a lot to set Werewolf apart, not just from other WoD games, but from other roleplaying games in general. In contrast, W5 feels a lot more generic and lacks a strong identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of my issue is that my first &quot;real&quot; exposure to Pentex was Pentex: Monkeywrenchers and the Book of Wyrm. Later, I really enjoyed Pentex's role in Project: Twilight. The thing is, none of those books really emphasized Pentex as a &quot;humorous&quot; corporation and the later satire of things kind of blew past me.<br /> <br /> For me, there's nothing really any more &quot;funny&quot; or &quot;silly&quot; about Pentex than Arasaka in Cyberpunk 2020 or Weyland-Yutani in Alien.<br /> <br /> It's there to be the Technocracy or Sabbat of the game and provide an immense amount of foes for our heroes to fight with unlimited resources. They're also a lot more interesting villains than Black Spiral Dancers or Nephandi.<br /> <br /> Very few people can understand, &quot;I want to unmake reality&quot; as a motive but everyone can understand, &quot;I want to make a shit ton of money.&quot; The irony being that Pentex has aged much better than most groups and with a bit of tweaking you could have them be the Seers of the Throne equivalent in Mage where they'd arguably fit just as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T17:38:22-08:00","id":1528506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528495#post1528495\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think part of my issue is that my first &quot;real&quot; exposure to Pentex was Pentex: Monkeywrenchers and the Book of Wyrm. Later, I really enjoyed Pentex's role in Project: Twilight. The thing is, none of those books really emphasized Pentex as a &quot;humorous&quot; corporation and the later satire of things kind of blew past me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally I found Pentex: Monkeywrenchers to be pretty damn funny. Just go look at the &quot;Endron Brochure&quot; in the back of the book, an in-setting Endron brochure aimed at the general public (and especially kids) to convince them that oil extraction is good, that Endron has done more to protect the planet than every environmental group combined, that their big Alaskan oil spill actually improved the environment, and it even and includes &quot;Planet Man&quot; Endron's mascot (and obvious Captain Planet reference). That kind of garbage is overblown, but it mirrors the sort of rhetoric you would see from Exxon and other oil companies, so the parody and humor was spot on.<br /> <br /> And we see that with all of the other subsidiaries - RED Network, O'Tolley's, King Brewery and whatnot. It's clear Pentex was always intended as a satire of corporations and corporate culture, as well as intended to be a punching bag for players to take their frustrations out on. Yeah, it's evil and what they do is serious, but there was also a meta-humor involved with them that set Werewolf (due to Pentex positioned as one of the primary villains of the setting) as a game with more humor in it than any of the other WoD games. You would never see something like that Endron Brochure in the other WoD games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T17:40:42-08:00","id":1528507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528506#post1528506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally I found Pentex: Monkeywrenchers to be pretty damn funny. Just go look at the &quot;Endron Brochure&quot; in the back of the book, an in-setting Endron brochure aimed at the general public (and especially kids) to convince them that oil extraction is good, that Endron has done more to protect the planet than every environmental group combined, that their big Alaskan oil spill actually improved the environment, and it even and includes &quot;Planet Man&quot; Endron's mascot (and obvious Captain Planet reference). That kind of garbage is overblown, but it mirrors the sort of rhetoric you would see Exxon and other oil companies, so the parody and humor was spot on.</div> </div> </div> </div>This may be a cultural thing but I grew up in West Virginia.<br /> <br /> None of that is satirical.<br /> <br /> In my local museum, we have a Daycare Center about teaching kids the value of coal mining and what a wonderful environmentally safe community the local oil business created.<br /> <br /> So, I'm not sure what the satire is when it's just an accurate depiction of how cynical, manipulative, and corrupt the industry is in RL. Indeed, things like Captain Planet in RL were actually meant to shift the idea of environmental protection from corporate regulation to individual responsibility (which does nothing to alleviate actual environmental devastation).<br /> <br /> I suppose it's one of those cases where I don't get the &quot;humor&quot; because the RL corporate culture of many places is beyond parody.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-13-2024, 08:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T19:05:55-08:00","id":1528513,"title":"","content":"Absolutely. As a fellow person who grew up in Appalachia/Appalachia-adjacent, look into the history of things like company towns and the efforts coal and oil companies go through to downplay how horrible and cartoonishly-evil these industries are. As extreme as Pentex is, and you do need these proxies with a cosmic evil attached to them to make them work as a <i>game</i>, but it's not as much of an exaggeration or parody as one might think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28155-gh0st-fox","name":"gh0st-fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar28155_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T19:18:02-08:00","id":1528514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gh0st-fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528513#post1528513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Absolutely. As a fellow person who grew up in Appalachia/Appalachia-adjacent, look into the history of things like company towns and the efforts coal and oil companies go through to downplay how horrible and cartoonishly-evil these industries are. As extreme as Pentex is, and you do need these proxies with a cosmic evil attached to them to make them work as a <i>game</i>, but it's not as much of an exaggeration or parody as one might think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have no shit met a Country Club fundamentalist guy who believed destroying the environment was what Jesus wanted so it would bring the Rapture earlier.<br /> <br /> After that point, I was like, &quot;Wow, Pentex is just accurate.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T19:51:07-08:00","id":1528515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528507#post1528507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This may be a cultural thing but I grew up in West Virginia.<br /> <br /> None of that is satirical.<br /> <br /> In my local museum, we have a Daycare Center about teaching kids the value of coal mining and what a wonderful environmentally safe community the local oil business created.<br /> <br /> So, I'm not sure what the satire is when it's just an accurate depiction of how cynical, manipulative, and corrupt the industry is in RL. Indeed, things like Captain Planet in RL were actually meant to shift the idea of environmental protection from corporate regulation to individual responsibility (which does nothing to alleviate actual environmental devastation).<br /> <br /> I suppose it's one of those cases where I don't get the &quot;humor&quot; because the RL corporate culture of many places is beyond parody.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean they clearly took the basic concept of corporate culture and corporate actions and then pushed them to the extreme to create a satire (look at Black Dog Game Studio or King Brewery's reflection onto frat culture), but that sort of satirical humor isn't for everyone. And, of course, there are area where real life is worse than satire, but that's often the case with satire. <br /> <br /> Regardless, the subsidiaries no longer appear to exist in W5, the satire is gone, so the characters will be dealing with more realistic companies like Exxon or McDonalds instead of Endron or O'Tolley's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T19:59:00-08:00","id":1528516,"title":"","content":"Captain Planet never tore off Looten Plunder's arms and watched him bleed out, but for Garou, that's Tuesday.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528514#post1528514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no shit met a Country Club fundamentalist guy who believed destroying the environment was what Jesus wanted so it would bring the Rapture earlier.<br /> <br /> After that point, I was like, &quot;Wow, Pentex is just accurate.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, right? Pentex shot for over the top parody, but you can't manage that, because people took the &quot;unrealistic parody&quot; POV and ran with it, even further past sense, because cultural shifts are like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T20:07:57-08:00","id":1528517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528515#post1528515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean they clearly took the basic concept of corporate culture and corporate actions and then pushed them to the extreme to create a satire (look at Black Dog Game Studio or King Brewery's reflection onto frat culture), but that sort of satirical humor isn't for everyone. And, of course, there are area where real life is worse than satire, but that's often the case with satire.<br /> <br /> Regardless, the subsidiaries no longer appear to exist in W5, the satire is gone, so the characters will be dealing with more realistic companies like Exxon or McDonalds instead of Endron or O'Tolley's.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean they list some subsidiaries. They even talk about a fake British Petroleum.<ul><li>Albion Petroleum, operating off the Irish coasts with drilling leases that never seem to expire, despite local sentiment being 80 percent against their renewal.</li> <li>Biblios (formerly known as Chi, formerly known as Xenophon Security), a consumer data aggregator.</li> <li>Scheldes Pharmaceuticals, running clinical trials across North America, moving operations state to state and territory to territory when local legal burdens make relocation prudent.</li> </ul>Plus, you kill Endron Employees in Earthblood.<br /> <br /> They just are getting a kind of weird, &quot;I mean you COULD use Albion Petroleum but why not use BP instead?&quot;<br /> <br /> And I'm like, &quot;I dunno, because it's not fun murdering BP employees?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-13T21:18:22-08:00","id":1528522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528507#post1528507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, things like Captain Planet in RL were actually meant to shift the idea of environmental protection from corporate regulation to individual responsibility (which does nothing to alleviate actual environmental devastation).</div> </div> </div> </div>To come back to this, I have to disagree with that. The explicit goal in Captain Planet was that Ted Turner wanted to foster an awareness in kids about the importance of environmentalism, and the idea that just because a problem is happening on the other side of the world doesn't mean it won't affect you.<br /> <br /> In quite a few episodes, Captain Planet and the kids couldn't solve the problem by themselves, but needed the help of local communities to come together to help fix the problem, showcasing the importance of community activism. Or conversely, you'd have episodes where at the end (after Captain Planet fought off the magical bad guys) the EPA would show up, because they were contacted earlier in the episode, to help shut down whatever polluting system was going on. Further, at the end of every episode they'd have suggestions on things that viewers (kids) could do to help, and this would often involve things like writing to politicians, boycotting companies that don't have good environmental policies, encouraging older adults who can vote to vote for pro-environmental policies, engaging in local community based activism to help get local pro-environmental changes, put together food drives, etc.<br /> <br /> Hell, one of the most reocurring themes was that individuals can't beat corporations on their own. When one of the Planeteers would go of in their own to fix a problem, they'd lose. You can't summon Captain Planet on your own. The show always pushed the need for collaborative activism to defeat corporate maleficence.<br /> <br /> Honestly I think the show was incredibly progressive, and I don't really see that it intended to shift the idea away from corporate regulation to individual responsibility, especially as the villains were corporations and there was almost always a point within the show that they were explicitly dodging environmental regulations. I guess there could be a cynical interpretation, but again, I don't think it really holds up too well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 01-14-2024, 12:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T01:28:24-08:00","id":1528527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528467#post1528467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's not even the patron it should be, but apparently they don't like the idea of Corporate versions of City Fathers/Mothers in the W5 development team.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a shame, because that's basically how modern corpos work. Instead of Evil Comic Book CEO you have a mass of worshipers in the form of investors and shareholders whose will is channeled through a high priest caste of directors, creating some kind of gestalt entity (that is even legally a person) who runs the whole show and shifts personal responsibility together with moral and ethical concerns away from actual humans. Decisions are much less the result of any individual, but manifest as demands of [The Company] gestalt.<br /> <br /> Maybe the idea for W5 was to put the concept that individuals are never directly responsible for the evil actions of a company in the front and it conflicted with the comic book villain approach for Pentex that older editions took, but I think in this case it would be easy to have both. At the end of the day, <i>someone </i>needs to sign that contract to manufacture Agent Orange, poison the ground water, or send a team of thugs who beat up the competition. You can absolutely have your corrupted board of directors that act like comic book villains, because real life has those, too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-14T06:08:40-08:00","id":1528540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528514#post1528514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have no shit met a Country Club fundamentalist guy who believed destroying the environment was what Jesus wanted so it would bring the Rapture earlier.<br /> <br /> After that point, I was like, &quot;Wow, Pentex is just accurate.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I remember chatting with a friend during the latter part of 2010s and going &quot;Wow, we are living in WoD now,huh?&quot;<br /> <br /> And I do think it does kind of make things weird to write, because how do you go darker from here without becoming a farce? Just from US elections, we have the side that accepts global warming and the side that does not. Nevermind January 6th.<br /> <br /> All the tools I used to make WoD WoD are now reality and that is scary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T15:06:13-08:00","id":1528684,"title":"","content":"This is going to sound ridiculous but I always felt like it was a missed opportunity not to have player character rules for Pentex. There's Freak Legion but I feel like they came THIS CLOSE to doing so with the Book of the Wyrm Pentex stories. You could be a lowly corporate cog or mercenary playing the deadly games of trying to advance in the world of high finance with occult stuff. If you can play a Technocrat or a Sabbat, you can play a Pentex operative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T16:30:31-08:00","id":1528686,"title":"","content":"There's bound to be problems with any book about environment and consequences of living in the world we live in that start with the line:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Companies aren\u2019t themselves bad by definition. Companies represent one approach to large-scale cooperation. Even accumulations of capital aren\u2019t inherently bad, so long as they\u2019re put to positive use. </div> </div> </div>It's a level of &quot;Oh we know we belong to a huge corporation that makes money on selling dreams and micro transactions, let's make sure they don't get cross if they feel called out.<br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528684#post1528684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is going to sound ridiculous but I always felt like it was a missed opportunity not to have player character rules for Pentex. There's Freak Legion but I feel like they came THIS CLOSE to doing so with the Book of the Wyrm Pentex stories. You could be a lowly corporate cog or mercenary playing the deadly games of trying to advance in the world of high finance with occult stuff. If you can play a Technocrat or a Sabbat, you can play a Pentex operative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeeeeeeeh. Why? Sabbat is alien, but at the end of the day they want humans to stick around and have ideals that might actually keep the world going instead of drowining in the blood of the Antedelluvians. Technocracy, as much as you prefer them as the 1E goons, has evolved into heroes with a checkered past that needs to own up to its mistakes if it's to make the world better. In some ways just like the Garou.<br /> <br /> On the other hand - Pentex are just absolutley amoral humans who exploit other people to profit. There's no special rules for that, It's just horrible people doing horrible things. Just because some of them happen to sell their souls or traffic with alien entities is the least of what defines them and if you had to is easily mapped to Gifts and Rites.<br /> <br /> Not that Fomori, BSD's or Pentex should be considered playable factions as they bring nothing useful to the table except for suffering porn for the maladjusted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-16T19:29:09-08:00","id":1528698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528686#post1528686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeeeeeeeh. Why? Sabbat is alien, but at the end of the day they want humans to stick around and have ideals that might actually keep the world going instead of drowining in the blood of the Antedelluvians. Technocracy, as much as you prefer them as the 1E goons, has evolved into heroes with a checkered past that needs to own up to its mistakes if it's to make the world better. In some ways just like the Garou.<br /> <br /> On the other hand - Pentex are just absolutley amoral humans who exploit other people to profit. There's no special rules for that, It's just horrible people doing horrible things. Just because some of them happen to sell their souls or traffic with alien entities is the least of what defines them and if you had to is easily mapped to Gifts and Rites.<br /> <br /> Not that Fomori, BSD's or Pentex should be considered playable factions as they bring nothing useful to the table except for suffering porn for the maladjusted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh,<br /> <br /> I'd argue that the Sabbat are worse than Pentex by far as they want to shove humans in pens and engage in horrific torture games with humans. For even the majority of Pentex employees &quot;in the know&quot;, they're unaware the goal is to destroy humanity. Pentex's executives think they're going to take over the world not kill everyone. It's a bit like the Wheel of Time. Ishmael is the only one of the Forsaken who believes the Dark One wants to annihilate everything versus world domination.<br /> <br /> But that's not really the point of a Pentex game. You'd absolutely be playing the villains in that. It'd just be about playing the fun complicated politics, mad science, and backstabbing of working for a megacorp. Just like working for Arasaka or one of the corporations in Cyberpunk 2020. You're absolutely evil but you're working for that $$$.<br /> <br /> The joy of Grand Theft Auto with suits.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T00:22:42-08:00","id":1528703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528684#post1528684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is going to sound ridiculous but I always felt like it was a missed opportunity not to have player character rules for Pentex. There's Freak Legion but I feel like they came THIS CLOSE to doing so with the Book of the Wyrm Pentex stories. You could be a lowly corporate cog or mercenary playing the deadly games of trying to advance in the world of high finance with occult stuff. If you can play a Technocrat or a Sabbat, you can play a Pentex operative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is most Pentex employees are just regular humans, and you can make regular humans already - no need for a new splat or book or rules. If you want to make them more supernatural there's stuff like hedge mages or fomori. I can understand why they never really spent word count making rules for Pentex player characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-17T08:15:39-08:00","id":1528715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1528427-w5-complaint-the-handling-of-pentex?p=1528703#post1528703\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is most Pentex employees are just regular humans, and you can make regular humans already - no need for a new splat or book or rules. If you want to make them more supernatural there's stuff like hedge mages or fomori. I can understand why they never really spent word count making rules for Pentex player characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>This and there is also the aspect of tone.<br /> <br /> Sabbat vs Camarilla is an ideological fight. Hide or openly rule, deny the ancients or try to hunt them. VtM is based on the choices the undead make to justify their existence.<br /> <br /> Techies vs Traditions is about freedom versus safety. Sure, freedom sounds good but then you consider that it comes with the very real danger of being eaten by a griffon. Safety meanwhile means that everything has a sense of logic to it and society trucks on expected paths, which can be stifling to creativity.<br /> <br /> Gaians vs the Wyrm is protecting nature and the health of the world vs destroying or corrupting it for a nihilistic agenda or for profit. There are shades of gray there, but most of it is pretty clearly lined as life vs destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}